<h1>The State Pension: what people receive and why</h1>

<p class="lede">The two headline rates are full rates: many people get less and some get more, because the amount depends on a person's National Insurance record and on which of the two systems they are on, set by date of birth and, for some, by sex. The State Pension is a regular payment from the government to people who have reached State Pension age.</p>

{% call m.note("This page explains the rules. It cannot tell you what you will get", 2, "not-a-personal-check") %}
<p>For your own amount, use the official services: <a href="https://www.gov.uk/check-state-pension">check your State Pension forecast</a>, <a href="https://www.gov.uk/state-pension-age">check your State Pension age</a> and <a href="https://www.gov.uk/check-national-insurance-record">check your National Insurance record</a>, all on GOV.UK.</p>
{% endcall %}

